# `to_int` (truncating; out of range aborts) — spec line 150.
#
# The check is `!(v >= -0x1p63 && v < 0x1p63)`, and it is written that way because
# two plausible spellings are WRONG: `v <= (double)INT64_MAX` accepts 2^63,
# because that cast rounds UP, and `v > -9223372036854775809.0` rejects INT64_MIN.
# On arm64 an unchecked cast does not trap — `fcvtzs` saturates — so the abort is
# the only thing standing between this and a silent INT64_MAX.
# Bulk regression case.

function main()
    print(to_int(1.5))
    print(to_int(9223372036854774784.0))
    print(to_int(9223372036854775808.0))
